 "notes": "DATA ONLY until the M6 trainer flags (--tight-cost / --tight-min-len / --death-mass-mult, branch m6-reward) are merged: gpu_run_v2 refuses to launch while the committed trainer lacks them. Image: devel (gcc) so --compile-learner reduce-overhead compiles (the runtime image falls back to eager; research/perf_quiet_20261013 RESULTS, branch perf-integrate-results). mac_rate 5,400/s: quiet-Mac end-to-end B8 + numba v61 + --learner-fast --obs-pack --batch-scale 2 (128x2: 5,364/s; 256x3: 5,337/s), rounded up. Sizing: vcpu_per_run 4.3 = learner + 3 actors (pods are actor-bound: 3-4 actors/run); ram_per_run_gb 8 = perf-ram --obs-pack (6.6 GB b / 5.5 GB bv8 per run) + a third CUDA actor; ring_gb_per_run 2.6 = packed bv8 rings for 3 actors x 128 worlds (2.52 GB, train_m3c.ring_nbytes). Initial wave on the 125 GB / 36 vCPU minimum: min(RAM 14, CPU 8, cap 10) = 8 runs. vram_per_run_gb 2.8 is an estimate (pod telemetry: 2.0 GB per run with a CUDA learner + 2 CUDA actors -> ~0.67 GB per CUDA process; + CUDA-graph pool, unmeasured): 8 x 2.8 = 22.4 of 24 GB, flagged by plan_warnings. G2: combined >= 21,600/s, and the pod's whole wall (create + upload + setup + 15 x 8M) must be <= 120M / 5,400 / 4 = 5,556 s (1.54 h). Launch amendment (2026-10-14): all arms add --gamma-start 0.998 --eps-end-at 1 (fine-tune starts at B8's end-of-schedule gamma/eps; m6-reward Stage-0 notes) and CTRL adds --tight-telemetry (same-seed tight_frac baseline, reward unchanged). max_concurrent_cap 7 (VRAM: 7 x 2.8 = 19.6 GB of 24). Attempt 1: host 35.02 cgroup CPUs < 36 -> deleted; min_vcpu 32 (7 runs x 4.3 = 30.1). Attempt 2 (04:00 PT): all 15 runs exited rc 1 within ~65 s (no outputs; the runner did not keep process logs; ~$0.33). Runner now pulls a failed run's log tail and runs an opt-in trainer preflight (run 0's exact argv, 30k transitions) before the wave.",
